# Append-only files: union merge instead of a conflict.
#
# Every branch appends at the same point, so two branches that share no
# product surface still collide on line N+1. Union merge keeps both sides'
# added lines. It is safe here precisely because these files are append-only
# and their invariants are checked elsewhere: a duplicate ledger id fails
# test-hooks.sh, so a bad union surfaces as a loud CI failure rather than a
# silent wrong merge.
#
# This does NOT apply to files where two edits can be semantically
# incompatible — those must still conflict and be resolved by a human.
.claude/memory/LEARNINGS.md merge=union
docs/DECISIONS.md            merge=union
